1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:08,150
Advanced effects are still effects: tasks, shared state, observation, time, and control flow of your own.

2
00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:15,100
Each one is answered by a handler. Stack the handlers, and they work on one program together.

3
00:00:16,750 --> 00:00:18,650
Three tasks share one counter.

4
00:00:18,650 --> 00:00:24,450
The state handler sits outside the scheduler, so every task reads and writes the same store.

5
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:32,167
A task runs until it waits. A Get and its Put, with no wait between them, are never split.

6
00:00:32,167 --> 00:00:34,900
A hundred each makes three hundred.

7
00:00:35,550 --> 00:00:41,083
Wait between the Get and the Put, and the other tasks read the same old value.

8
00:00:41,083 --> 00:00:44,550
Two of every three updates are lost: one hundred.

9
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:51,600
Hold a semaphore of one across the read and the write, and the count is three hundred again.

10
00:00:54,250 --> 00:01:00,350
WithObserve shows you every effect that part of a program yields, without handling any of them.

11
00:01:01,250 --> 00:01:07,350
It sees the effects of tasks spawned inside its scope, and nothing yielded outside it.

12
00:01:08,250 --> 00:01:14,350
Each effect still goes on to its handler. The result and the log are the same as without the observer.

13
00:01:16,750 --> 00:01:23,600
Control flow of your own is a handler for an effect of your own. Audit and Abort are plain data classes.

14
00:01:24,350 --> 00:01:29,000
The Audit handler resumes k, so checkout goes on after the Audit.

15
00:01:29,750 --> 00:01:31,883
The Abort handler never resumes k.

16
00:01:31,883 --> 00:01:37,000
The body ends right where it yielded Abort, and the handler's value is the result.

17
00:01:37,750 --> 00:01:44,600
With stock, checkout returns ordered. Without, the result is: aborted, out of stock.

18
00:01:46,250 --> 00:01:52,200
Time is effects too. Delay and GetTime mean what the time handler says.

19
00:01:52,950 --> 00:01:57,533
Under the sync handler, a one and a half second Delay sleeps for real.

20
00:01:57,533 --> 00:02:04,100
Under the simulated clock, the clock moves, and the run takes under a millisecond, even for an hour.

21
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:11,600
doeff: tasks, state, observation, time and your own control flow are all effects,

22
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:17,250
and the handlers you stack decide what each one does. pip install doeff.
